/// @yah:gotcha("TWO LIMITS OF THIS FIX A LATER READER MUST NOT OVERREAD. (1) OpenFlags::ReadOnly does NOT escape turso's process-global registry: Database::open_file_with_flags consults DATABASE_MANAGER keyed by file id BEFORE it looks at the flags (turso_core-0.7.2/lib.rs:940) and returns an already-open Database with the caller's flags DISCARDED. So inside one process that already holds a writable handle on the same file, open_reader silently gives you that writable handle -- the same trap snapshot.rs's upload_base_snapshot doc already records for roadcase. Cross-process (the headscale case, and every case this ticket is about) is unaffected. (2) The validation detects a fold that overlaps the copy; it does not prevent one, and it cannot make a sufficiently hot database backupable. Probe H's HOT regime refuses 9 of 12 copies by design. If a real workload lands there the answer is a different cadence or a bigger COPY_VALIDATION_ATTEMPTS, decided from measurement -- NOT loosening stable_across, which is the one thing standing between this and the torn image the ticket calls strictly worse.")
